<div id="algx1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l21.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="algx1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}=\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}(z_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}=\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algx1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="algx1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we first review background on latent diffusion models, classifier-free guidance, and CLIP encoders (Sec.<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Preliminaries ‣ 3 Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure ‣ Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>). We then introduce our formulation of concept prototypes (Sec.<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Concept Prototype ‣ 3 Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure ‣ Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>), followed by how these prototypes are used as guidance signals to steer diffusion models away from the target concept during inference (Sec. <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Concept Erasure with Prototype Guidance ‣ 3 Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure ‣ Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our method builds upon latent diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> guided by text embeddings and leverages the text–image alignment established by CLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. We briefly review these foundations below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Latent Diffusion Models</span>.
Diffusion models learn a target data distribution through iterative denoising <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>.
Latent diffusion models (LDMs) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> improve efficiency by operating in the latent space.
Given an image <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, its latent representation is encoded through a pretrained variational autoencoder (VAE) encoder <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\mathcal{E}_{\text{VAE}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\mathcal{E}_{\text{VAE}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is progressively noised into <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> across timesteps <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
An LDM parameterized by <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> predicts the added noise <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on an optional text prompt <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
The training objective of an LDM is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{LDM}}=\mathbb{E}_{z_{t},c,\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)}\big[\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)\|^{2}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>LDM</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{LDM}}=\mathbb{E}_{z_{t},c,\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)}\big[\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)\|^{2}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">During inference, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> is iteratively denoised to obtain <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is eventually decoded back to image space as <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}(z_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> through the image decoder of LDM.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Classifier-free Guidance</span> (CFG) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> enables controllable generation without external classifiers.
By contrasting the denoising predictions between the conditional and unconditional samplings, the adjusted score <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is guided with scale <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> towards the semantics specified by the text prompt <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(z_{t},c)=\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})+\alpha\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(z_{t},c)=\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})+\alpha\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLIP Encoders</span>.
LDMs commonly adopt its pretrained text encoder <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{T}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐓</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{T}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> from CLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>, which provides a shared embedding space jointly learned with an image encoder <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{I}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{I}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. CLIP’s large-scale contrastive pretraining yields robust cross-modal alignment, making its encoders well-suited for conditioning LDMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> and for measuring image-text correspondence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. In practice, the cosine similarity between CLIP image and text embeddings is widely used as a standard metric of semantic alignment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Concept Prototype</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Broad concepts exhibit high-variety and multi-faceted structure that cannot be represented by a single direction in the embedding space.
We thus capture their diversity through a set of <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">concept prototypes</span> drawn from both the image and text embedding spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, for a given target concept <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we begin by collecting a set of text prompts containing related semantics of size <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since these prompts may include information irrelevant or orthogonal to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct a <span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">concept-contrastive prompt set</span> in which each prompt retains all contextual content but omits <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.
For example, removing concept “sexual” from the following prompt changes its expression from red-highlighted to blue-highlighted text, while keeping other descriptive content unchanged:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">documentary style an adult couple in a dressing room, <span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_sout" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">artistic nude silhouette</span> <span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">casual clothing</span>, overcast soft light, over-the-shoulder shot.</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and its concept-contrastive counterpart <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> images with and without the target concept <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.
Each image (either <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,k}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,k}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>) is encoded by the CLIP image encoder, and we compute all pairwise differences between the two embedding sets:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{diff}}=\big\{\,z_{i,j}-z^{-}_{i,k}\;\big|\;1\leq i\leq N,\;1\leq j,k\leq M\big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{diff}}=\big\{\,z_{i,j}-z^{-}_{i,k}\;\big|\;1\leq i\leq N,\;1\leq j,k\leq M\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain representative semantic directions, we apply a clustering operator <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{\text{diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mtext>diff</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{\text{diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce a set of <span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">image concept prototypes</span>:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(1)},\dots,p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(K)}\}=\mathsf{K}(\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{diff}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(1)},\dots,p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(K)}\}=\mathsf{K}(\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{diff}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where each prototype <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a cluster centroid capturing one expressive mode of the concept in the image embedding space of dimension <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To enable direct control over LDMs, which are conditioned on text prompts, we have to transfer the image-space prototypes into text domain.
We construct a set of <span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">textual concept prototypes</span>, where each prototype is a learnable soft prompt <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> learnable token embeddings, equivalently serving as a length-<math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> prompt for conditioning the LDM.
To perform this cross-modal transfer, we take advantage of the pretrained CLIP text encoder, which offers strong text–image alignment and is already used as the conditioning module in standard LDMs.
To pair each textual prototype <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> with its counterpart image prototype <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the following optimization problem by maximizing their cosine similarity in the aligned embedding space:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}}\;\frac{\langle p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)},\,\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})\rangle}{\|p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)}\|\;\|\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}}\;\frac{\langle p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)},\,\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})\rangle}{\|p_{\mathbf{I}}^{(k)}\|\;\|\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a differentiable mapping that projects a textual embedding into the joint CLIP embedding space.
Specifically, <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by feeding <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> into the CLIP text encoder and extracting the End-of-Text (EoT) token embedding, which CLIP uses as a global summary of the entire sequence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
Through the encoder’s attention layers, information from all token positions is naturally aggregated into this final embedding, allowing gradients to flow back through the frozen encoder and update only the learnable prompt parameters in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
After convergence, the optimized <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> serves as a text-space concept prototype representing the semantic mode associated with concept <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Concept Erasure with Prototype Guidance</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During inference, given a textual prompt <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> that may contain the undesirable concept <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we identify the prototype most relevant to the prompt.
Specifically, we compute the cosine similarity between the embedding of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and each textual prototype, and select the top-1 prototype whose similarity exceeds a threshold <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}k^{\ast}&amp;=\arg\max_{k\in\{1,\ldots,K\}}\;\cos\!\big(\mathcal{E}(c),\,\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})\big)\\
&amp;\text{s.t.}\quad\cos\!\big(\mathcal{E}(c),\,\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k^{\ast})})\big)\geq\tau.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.046em;" width="1.046em"><mi>cos</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.046em;" width="1.046em"><mi>cos</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}k^{\ast}&amp;=\arg\max_{k\in\{1,\ldots,K\}}\;\cos\!\big(\mathcal{E}(c),\,\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k)})\big)\\
&amp;\text{s.t.}\quad\cos\!\big(\mathcal{E}(c),\,\mathcal{E}(p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k^{\ast})})\big)\geq\tau.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If no prototype satisfies the threshold criterion, no negative guidance is applied.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To suppress the generation of undesirable concept, we extend standard classifier-free guidance by incorporating the selected textual prototype <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k^{\ast})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k^{\ast})}</annotation></semantics></math> as a negative conditioning signal, with scale <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. The modified denoising prediction becomes:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(z_{t},c)=&amp;\overbrace{\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})+\alpha\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})\big)}^{\text{standard CFG}}\\
&amp;\underbrace{-\beta\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k^{\ast})}-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})\big)}_{\text{negative prototype guidance}},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mover><mover accent="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏞</mo></mover><mtext>standard CFG</mtext></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>negative prototype guidance</mtext></munder><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\tilde{\epsilon}_{\theta}(z_{t},c)=&amp;\overbrace{\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})+\alpha\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},c)-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})\big)}^{\text{standard CFG}}\\
&amp;\underbrace{-\beta\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},p_{\mathbf{T}}^{(k^{\ast})}-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t})\big)}_{\text{negative prototype guidance}},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To summarize the whole procedure, Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure ‣ Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> outlines the full pipeline of Prototype-Guided Concept Erasure.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S3.T1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Performance comparison of baselines on the I2P dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> for broad-concept removal<span id="S3.T1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. We report the proportion of generated images flagged as <span id="S3.T1.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">inappropriate</span> by the Q16 detector <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>. Results marked with * are sourced from TRCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>. </span>Bold<span id="S3.T1.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> indicates the best performance and <span id="S3.T1.8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underline</span> indicates the second-best.</span></span></figcaption>
